# Merged from the former .gitignore.txt, which was never active: with a .txt
# suffix Git ignored the file itself, so none of its research-data rules had
# any effect. Nothing sensitive was ever committed (checked against the full
# history), but nothing was stopping it either. Everything below is now live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit research data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/participants/
/transcripts/
/recordings/
/screening/
*.consent.pdf

# NVivo project files - these embed coded transcript text, not just analysis
*.nvp
*.nvpx

# Qualtrics exports: screening responses carry participant contact details.
# Root-anchored, so a stray export dropped in the repo root cannot be added by
# accident, while a legitimate data file inside a subfolder is still possible.
/*.csv
/*.tsv
/*.xlsx
/*.xls

# Session artefacts - Teams recordings and transcripts. Deliberately not
# root-anchored: a recording is sensitive wherever it lands.
*.mp4
*.m4a
*.vtt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy and secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vercel
.env*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# Both spellings on purpose: this repo uses .screenshots/, the old file said
# /screenshots/, and neither covered the other.
.screenshots
/screenshots/

# Also covered by the user-level ignore file, but repeated here so protection
# does not depend on one machine's global Git config.
.claude/settings.local.json
